 "notes": "All five planned kinds kept (Gin, Genever, Vodka, Flavoured vodka, Aquavit); gin and vodka styles/bases moved into 't'. Old vodka duplicates 'Alexander Vodka' / 'Alexandrion Saber Distilleries 1789 Alexander Vodka' merged. Old makerless models became versions of archetypes. Monkey 47: no Wikipedia page exists and the Pernod (theabsolutcompany.com) page returned 403; sourced from Difford's Guide, launch year left blank (not on that page). Gordon's year 1769 per its article (Gin article says 1763). Sloe gin left to the Liqueurs shelf. Genever archetypes are the legal styles (oude, jonge, korenwijn) with Bols and Zuidam bottlings as versions; no Bols Genever launch year found. Left out: Sipsmith, Nicholson's, Russian Standard, Beluga, Løiten, Lysholm, Bommerlunder (named on retrieved pages but no detail worth an archetype); Elyx and Burrough's Reserve not confirmed by retrieved pages. No traditions added (industrial spirits; genever GI noted as types)."
